Terse keywords
description: yaml-style short names, probably kebab-cased - TBD
- >
  JSON Schema's keywords are verbose and camel-cased (`additionalProperties`, `minItems`,
  `uniqueItems`). Yamlover meta keywords are **YAML-style short** - the tradition of `set`,
  `omap`, `int` - and compound ones probably **kebab-cased**. The **type names are ruled**
  (2026-08-09): `str`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `null`, `binary`, `leaf`; `map`, `seq`, `kseq`,
  `vmap`, `vseq`, `omni` ([the cube](*::meta:facets)) - the long JSON-Schema spellings read
  forever as aliases. The **member clauses are ruled** (2026-08-14): the omni
  [`members:`](*::meta:members) clause with its `others:` sweep replaces
  `properties`/`items`/`prefixItems`/`additionalProperties` - legacy read forever. The remaining
  keyword spellings (kebab-case for compounds, the quantifiers) are TBD, and the
  [equivalence table](*::meta:vs-json-schema) tracks each keyword's fate.
